Z||000000||Fformula88||11-11-2000||10:58 AM||||My dads 87 coupe has a small hole started on the drivers side floor board.  I want to get it fixed before the snow flies (and the roads are covered with salt!)  I cannot decide on what to try and use, so I wanted to get everyone's opinion.  Whats the best way to patch this hole?  Its about the size of a nickel... and I'd say there is about anotther quarter inch of bad metal around it that would have to be removed.  So its not a big hole.  Thanx in advance!||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-11-2000||11:37 AM||||remove the rusted area and clean to bare metal around the hole on the bottom of the car. leave it rough. hit it with some 60-80 grit to make it rough. (Doing it from the bottom saves pulling the carpets.)<P>epoxy a patch over the hole from the bottom. put the adhesive around the edges of the patch and push it in place. hold it still untill the epoxy sets.<P>once the epoxy has cured coat it with something to prevent more rust. ||||reg||1
